`DataContainer.observation_frame()` is removed in favour of `obs_table()`, which did the same job; use `obs_table(include_ids=True, id_col="sample_id")` for the old `sample_id` column. `obs_table()` keeps each coordinate's dtype (a numeric coordinate used to come back as `object`, which plots and numeric checks did not treat as numbers; tables written to parquet are unchanged) and always has one row per observation. The unused `verbose` argument of `TabularDataset.clean` is removed.
